encong Lin , cite56†Yifu Sun , cite57†Shirui Huang , cite58†Lin Niu , cite59†Gu Gong , cite60†Guojian Xiao , cite61†Bojian Zheng , cite62†Xiang Yuan , cite63†Qi Chen , cite64†Jie Xiao , cite65†Dongyang Zheng , cite42†Xiaofeng Yang , cite66†Kai Liu , cite67†Jianchen Zhu , cite68†Lifu Wang , cite69†Qinglin Lu , cite13†Jie Liu , cite70†Liang Dong , cite71†Fan Jiang , cite72†Ruibin Chen , cite68†Lei Wang , cite73†Chao Zhang , cite74†Jiaxin Lin , cite75†Hao Zhang , cite76†Zheng Ye , cite77†Peng He , cite78†Runzhou Wu , cite79†Yinhe Wu , cite80†Jiayao Du , cite81†Jupeng Chen , cite82†Xinyue Mao , cite83†Dongyuan Guo , cite84†Yixuan Tang , cite85†Yulin Tsai , cite86†Yonghao Tan , cite87†Jiaao Yu , cite87†Junlin Yu , cite88†Keren Zhang , cite6†Yifan Li , cite89†Peng Chen , cite90†Tian Liu , cite91†Di Wang , cite92†Yuhong Liu , cite93†Linus , cite94†Jie Jiang , cite95†Zhuo Chen , cite96†Chunchao Guo L11: View a PDF of the paper titled Hunyuan3D Studio: End-to-End AI Pipeline for Game-Ready 3D Asset Generation, by Biwen Lei and 99 other authors\nL12: \nL13: cite97†View PDF cite98†HTML (experimental) L14: > Abstract:The creation of high-quality 3D assets, a cornerstone of modern game development, has long been characterized by labor-intensive and specialized workflows. This paper presents Hunyuan3D Studio, an end-to-end AI-powered content creation platform designed to revolutionize the game production pipeline by automating and streamlining the generation of game-ready 3D assets.\nL15: At its core, Hunyuan3D Studio integrates a suite of advanced neural modules (such as Part-level 3D Generation, Polygon Generation, Semantic UV, etc.) into a cohesive and user-friendly system. This unified framework allows for the rapid transformation of a single concept image or textual description into a fully-realized, production-quality 3D model complete with optimized geometry and high-fidelity PBR textures.\nL16: We demonstrate that assets generated by Hunyuan3D Studio are not only visually compelling but also adhere to the stringent technical requirements of contemporary game engines, significantly reducing iteration time and lowering the barrier to entry for 3D content creation. By providing a seamless bridge from creative intent to technical asset, Hunyuan3D Studio represents a significant leap forward for AI-assisted workflows in game development and interactive media.\nL17: Comments:  | Technical Report\nL18: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL19: Cite as:  | cite99†arXiv:2509.12815 [cs.CV]\nL20:    | (or cite100†arXiv:2509.12815v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL21:    | cite101†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2509.12815†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Biwen Lei [cite102†view email ]\nL25: [v1] Tue, 16 Sep 2025 08:33:03 UTC (45,937 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled Hunyuan3D Studio: End-to-End AI Pipeline for Game-Ready 3D Asset Generation, by Biwen Lei and 99 other authors\nL32: \nL33:   * cite97†View PDF L34:   * cite98†HTML (experimental) L35:   * cite103†TeX Source L36: \nL37: cite104†view license L38: ### Current browse context:\nL39: \nL40: cs.CV\nL41: \nL42: cite105†< prev |   cite106†next > L43: \nL44: cite107†new | cite108†recent | cite109†2025-09 L45: \nL46: Change to browse by:\nL47: \nL48: cite110†cs L49: \nL50: ### References & Citations\nL51: \nL52:   * cite111†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L53:   * cite112†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L54:   * cite113†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L55: \nL56: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL57: \nL58: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL59: \nL60: [Button: ×]\nL61: \nL62: loading...\nL63: \nL64: Data provided by:\nL65: \nL66: ### Bo