nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 16 Sep 2025]\nL9: # Title:3D Aware Region Prompted Vision Language Model\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†An-Chieh Cheng , cite6†Yang Fu , cite7†Yukang Chen , cite8†Zhijian Liu , cite9†Xiaolong Li , cite10†Subhashree Radhakrishnan , cite11†Song Han , cite12†Yao Lu , cite13†Jan Kautz , cite14†Pavlo Molchanov , cite15†Hongxu Yin , cite16†Xiaolong Wang , cite17†Sifei Liu L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled 3D Aware Region Prompted Vision Language Model, by An-Chieh Cheng and 12 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite18†View PDF cite19†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We present Spatial Region 3D (SR-3D) aware vision-language model that connects single-view 2D images and multi-view 3D data through a shared visual token space. SR-3D supports flexible region prompting, allowing users to annotate regions with bounding boxes, segmentation masks on any frame, or directly in 3D, without the need for exhaustive multi-frame labeling.\nL17: We achieve this by enriching 2D visual features with 3D positional embeddings, which allows the 3D model to draw upon strong 2D priors for more accurate spatial reasoning across frames, even when objects of interest do not co-occur within the same view. Extensive experiments on both general 2D vision language and specialized 3D spatial benchmarks demonstrate that SR-3D achieves state-of-the-art performance, underscoring its effectiveness for unifying 2D and 3D representation space on scene understanding.\nL18: Moreover, we observe applicability to in-the-wild videos without sensory 3D inputs or ground-truth 3D annotations, where SR-3D accurately infers spatial relationships and metric measurements.\nL19: Comments:  | Project Website: cite20†this https URL†www.anjiecheng.me L20: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL21: Cite as: